        "h": "Acute and sub-acute care",
        "list": [
          "Hospital care for acute illness carries special hazards for elders: delirium, deconditioning, falls, pressure injury, incontinence and adverse drug events ('hazards of hospitalisation').",
          "Principles: early mobilisation, orientation, avoid unnecessary catheters/lines/restraints, review medications, plan discharge from admission.",
          "Sub-acute/intermediate care bridges hospital and home for continued recovery."
        ]
