        "h": "Consent, capacity and confidentiality",
        "list": [
          "Informed consent requires that the person is competent, has adequate information, and decides voluntarily.",
          "Capacity is decision-specific and can fluctuate; cognitive impairment does not automatically mean incapacity — assess each decision.",
          "When a person lacks capacity, decisions are made in their best interest, involving family/surrogate and any advance wishes.",
          "Confidentiality and privacy must be maintained; information is shared only with consent or when safety requires it."
        ]
